# Dragon Magazine Compendium - features of the fighter variant classes (fv_build.py).

###Block: Fighter (Bodyguard)
Fighter (Bodyguard)	KEY:Fighter (Bodyguard) ~ Class Description	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	VISIBLE:NO	SOURCEPAGE:p.276	DESC:A specialist fighter (Dragon Magazine Compendium variant fighter): A warrior specifically trained to protect a charge: alert to ambushes, testing food for poison, identifying liars, often a skilled bargainer. Bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and every even level from the list of the Bodyguard Fighter Feat, or one of its special abilities in their place. 
Bonus Feats	KEY:Fighter (Bodyguard) ~ Bonus Feats	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	DEFINE:BodyguardBonusFeatCount|0	BONUS:VAR|BodyguardBonusFeatCount|1+floor(Bodyguard_FVLVL/2)	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Bodyguard Fighter Feat|BodyguardBonusFeatCount	SOURCEPAGE:p.276	DESC:Bonus feats from the bodyguard list, or special abilities in their place (%1 now).|BodyguardBonusFeatCount
Cover	KEY:Bodyguard Fighter ~ Cover	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantBodyguard	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Bodyguard)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.276	DESC:Bodyguard special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). As a free action the bodyguard gives an adjacent creature the benefit of her shield bonus to AC, or the dodge bonus of her Combat Expertise, or both (each to a different adjacent creature if she wishes); she then loses those bonuses herself. A protected creature moving more than 5 feet away loses the bonus at once. The bonuses stack with the protected creature's own.
Clear the Path	KEY:Bodyguard Fighter ~ Clear the Path	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantBodyguard	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Bodyguard)=1	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Cleave	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Great Cleave	SOURCEPAGE:p.276	DESC:Bodyguard special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). The bodyguard gains Cleave and Great Cleave (applied), but they only apply when she fights defensively, uses Combat Expertise, or gives her shield bonus to another creature with cover.

###Block: Fighter (Commander)
Fighter (Commander)	KEY:Fighter (Commander) ~ Class Description	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	VISIBLE:NO	SOURCEPAGE:p.276	DESC:A specialist fighter (Dragon Magazine Compendium variant fighter): Soldiers trained to recognize and use others' abilities in battle along with their own skill; they lead troops and companions. Bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and every even level from the list of the Commander Fighter Feat, or one of its special abilities in their place. 
Bonus Feats	KEY:Fighter (Commander) ~ Bonus Feats	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	DEFINE:CommanderBonusFeatCount|0	BONUS:VAR|CommanderBonusFeatCount|1+floor(Commander_FVLVL/2)	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Commander Fighter Feat|CommanderBonusFeatCount	SOURCEPAGE:p.276	DESC:Bonus feats from the commander list, or special abilities in their place (%1 now).|CommanderBonusFeatCount
Helpful Hints	KEY:Commander Fighter ~ Helpful Hints	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantCommander	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Commander)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.276	DESC:Commander special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). Surveying a fight, he uses the aid another action from up to 60 feet away (a standard action and a successful attack roll against AC 10 as normal): an ally in melee with an opponent gains +2 on her next attack roll against it, or +2 to AC against its next attack, before his next turn; the ally must hear and understand him.
Rousing Speech	KEY:Commander Fighter ~ Rousing Speech	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantCommander	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Commander)=1	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Commander)=2	SOURCEPAGE:p.276	DESC:Commander special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). A full-round action not provoking attacks of opportunity: allies within 60 feet gain a +1 morale bonus on attacks for 1 round if he succeeds on a DC 15 Diplomacy check, +1 round per point by which he exceeds the DC; once per day per two commander levels (%1/day now). Not before 2nd level.|floor(var("Commander_FVLVL")/2)

###Block: Fighter (Corsair)
Fighter (Corsair)	KEY:Fighter (Corsair) ~ Class Description	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	VISIBLE:NO	SOURCEPAGE:p.277	DESC:A specialist fighter (Dragon Magazine Compendium variant fighter): A marine warrior as deadly with her blade as any soldier and twice as dangerous in her home territory - the shifting decks and rigging of ships. Bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and every even level from the list of the Corsair Fighter Feat, or one of its special abilities in their place. Skill Focus is limited to a corsair class skill (by hand). She also gains one special ability for free at 1st and at 2nd level (Corsair Free Special Ability).
Bonus Feats	KEY:Fighter (Corsair) ~ Bonus Feats	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	DEFINE:CorsairBonusFeatCount|0	BONUS:VAR|CorsairBonusFeatCount|1+floor(Corsair_FVLVL/2)	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Corsair Fighter Feat|CorsairBonusFeatCount	SOURCEPAGE:p.277	DESC:Bonus feats from the corsair list, or special abilities in their place (%1 now).|CorsairBonusFeatCount
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Fighter (Corsair) ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|TYPE=Simple|TYPE=Martial	AUTO:ARMORPROF|ARMORTYPE=Light	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.277	DESC:Proficient with all simple and martial weapons, light armor and shields (except tower shields).
Climb-Fighting	KEY:Corsair Fighter ~ Climb-Fighting	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantCorsair	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Corsair)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.277	DESC:Corsair special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). So used to fighting in the rigging of a ship that she is no longer considered flat-footed when climbing.
Rope Movement	KEY:Corsair Fighter ~ Rope Movement	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantCorsair	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Corsair)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.277	DESC:Corsair special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). She may use Use Rope in place of Tumble to move through threatened areas where there is rigging, rope, vine or something similar to swing from; 5 or more ranks in Jump give a +2 synergy bonus on these checks.
Slow Fall	KEY:Corsair Fighter ~ Slow Fall	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantCorsair	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Corsair)=1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	SOURCEPAGE:p.277	DESC:Corsair special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). Within reach of a sail, tapestry or similar item, with a bladed weapon in hand, she drives the blade through the cloth and rides it down (or uses a rope or pole that fits her hand): the fall counts as 30 feet shorter per time this ability is taken (%1 feet now), only for the length of the cloth or rope; Jump and Tumble may shorten it further.|30*count("ABILITIES","KEY=Corsair Fighter ~ Slow Fall")
Swinging Bull Rush	KEY:Corsair Fighter ~ Swinging Bull Rush	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantCorsair	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Corsair)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.277	DESC:Corsair special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). Swinging from something while bull rushing: +1 on the opposed Strength check per 5 feet swung; if she wins, the opponent is pushed back an additional 5 feet without her following. It still provokes an attack of opportunity unless she has Improved Bull Rush.
Big Breath	KEY:Corsair Fighter ~ Big Breath	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantCorsair	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Corsair)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.277	DESC:Corsair special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). Once she must make Constitution checks to avoid drowning, she checks only every other round (the DC still rises by one per check).
Ocean Tangle	KEY:Corsair Fighter ~ Ocean Tangle	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantCorsair	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Corsair)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.277	DESC:Corsair special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). In water deep enough to swim, she can use a Swim check instead of a grapple check in any opposed grapple check.
Corsair Free Special Ability	KEY:Fighter (Corsair) ~ Corsair Free Special Ability	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Corsair Free Special Ability|(Corsair_FVLVL>=1)+(Corsair_FVLVL>=2)	SOURCEPAGE:p.277	DESC:one special ability for free at 1st and at 2nd level (%1 now).|(Corsair_FVLVL>=1)+(Corsair_FVLVL>=2)

###Block: Fighter (Exoticist)
Fighter (Exoticist)	KEY:Fighter (Exoticist) ~ Class Description	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	VISIBLE:NO	SOURCEPAGE:p.282	DESC:A specialist fighter (Dragon Magazine Compendium variant fighter): Fighters who forgo training in traditional, mundane weapons for the strange and exotic. Bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and every even level from the list of the Exoticist Fighter Feat, or one of its special abilities in their place. Weapon-specific bonus feats must name an exotic weapon she is proficient with (by hand). Her special abilities need an exotic weapon she is proficient with.
Bonus Feats	KEY:Fighter (Exoticist) ~ Bonus Feats	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	DEFINE:ExoticistBonusFeatCount|0	BONUS:VAR|ExoticistBonusFeatCount|1+floor(Exoticist_FVLVL/2)	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Exoticist Fighter Feat|ExoticistBonusFeatCount	SOURCEPAGE:p.282	DESC:Bonus feats from the exoticist list, or special abilities in their place (%1 now).|ExoticistBonusFeatCount
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Fighter (Exoticist) ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|TYPE=Simple	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy|TYPE=ShieldProfTower	SOURCEPAGE:p.282	DESC:Proficient with simple weapons, all armor (heavy, medium and light) and shields (including tower shields), and with four exotic weapons chosen at 1st level (Exoticist Exotic Weapons).
Dazzling Display	KEY:Exoticist Fighter ~ Dazzling Display	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantExoticist	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Exoticist)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.282	DESC:Exoticist special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). A flamboyant display of her exotic weapon hides her attack maneuvers: +4 on Bluff checks to feint in combat.
Exotic Attack	KEY:Exoticist Fighter ~ Exotic Attack	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantExoticist	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Exoticist)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.282	DESC:Exoticist special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). Wielding strange weapons strangely: +2 on opposed trip attempts she initiates with her exotic weapon and on opposed disarm rolls.
Strange Strike	KEY:Exoticist Fighter ~ Strange Strike	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantExoticist	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Exoticist)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.282	DESC:Exoticist special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). A +1 competence bonus on attack rolls if her opponent is not proficient with the exotic weapon she wields.
Exoticist Exotic Weapons	KEY:Fighter (Exoticist) ~ Exoticist Exotic Weapons	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Exoticist Exotic Weapons|4	SOURCEPAGE:p.282	DESC:Four exotic weapon proficiencies at 1st level.

###Block: Fighter (Fencer)
Fighter (Fencer)	KEY:Fighter (Fencer) ~ Class Description	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	VISIBLE:NO	SOURCEPAGE:p.282	DESC:A specialist fighter (Dragon Magazine Compendium variant fighter): A refined warrior who fights for pride and personal honor, trained in a specialized weapon style. Bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and every even level from the list of the Fencer Fighter Feat, or one of its special abilities in their place. Skill Focus is limited to a fencer class skill (by hand). Special abilities from 4th level.
Bonus Feats	KEY:Fighter (Fencer) ~ Bonus Feats	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	DEFINE:FencerBonusFeatCount|0	BONUS:VAR|FencerBonusFeatCount|1+floor(Fencer_FVLVL/2)	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Fencer Fighter Feat|FencerBonusFeatCount	SOURCEPAGE:p.282	DESC:Bonus feats from the fencer list, or special abilities in their place (%1 now).|FencerBonusFeatCount
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Fighter (Fencer) ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|TYPE=Simple|TYPE=Martial	AUTO:ARMORPROF|ARMORTYPE=Light	AUTO:SHIELDPROF|Buckler	SOURCEPAGE:p.282	DESC:Proficient with all simple and martial weapons, light armor and the buckler.
Encouraging Blow	KEY:Fencer Fighter ~ Encouraging Blow	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantFencer	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Fencer)=1	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Fencer)=4	SOURCEPAGE:p.282	DESC:Fencer special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). Whenever he scores a threat against an opponent (critical or not) he gains a +3 morale bonus to AC against that foe's attacks for rounds equal to his Charisma bonus (minimum 1), doubled if the threat becomes a critical; not against creatures with Intelligence below 3 or immune to mind-affecting effects.
Denigrating Banter	KEY:Fencer Fighter ~ Denigrating Banter	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantFencer	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Fencer)=1	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Fencer)=4	SOURCEPAGE:p.282	DESC:Fencer special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). As a standard action he baits and taunts a foe: opposed Charisma checks; if the foe fails, its base attack bonus is penalized by -2, -1 more per 5 points by which it failed (losing feats, abilities and attacks whose base attack minimum it no longer meets), for Charisma bonus + 1 rounds (minimum 1); not stacking; language-dependent, sonic, mind-affecting; %1/day (3 + Charisma bonus).|3+max(0,CHA)
Insurmountable Counter	KEY:Fencer Fighter ~ Insurmountable Counter	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantFencer	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Fencer)=1	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Fencer)=4	SOURCEPAGE:p.282	DESC:Fencer special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). Reading his opponent he nullifies one of its techniques: a +2 dodge bonus to AC when attacked by a foe using Power Attack or Combat Expertise.

###Block: Fighter (Horseman)
Fighter (Horseman)	KEY:Fighter (Horseman) ~ Class Description	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	VISIBLE:NO	SOURCEPAGE:p.284	DESC:A specialist fighter (Dragon Magazine Compendium variant fighter): Horsemen trade encumbering armor for enhanced mobility and a single devastating lance charge for a series of punishing ride-by attacks. Bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and every even level from the list of the Horseman Fighter Feat, or one of its special abilities in their place. 
Bonus Feats	KEY:Fighter (Horseman) ~ Bonus Feats	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	DEFINE:HorsemanBonusFeatCount|0	BONUS:VAR|HorsemanBonusFeatCount|1+floor(Horseman_FVLVL/2)	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Horseman Fighter Feat|HorsemanBonusFeatCount	SOURCEPAGE:p.284	DESC:Bonus feats from the horseman list, or special abilities in their place (%1 now).|HorsemanBonusFeatCount
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Fighter (Horseman) ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|TYPE=Simple|TYPE=Martial	AUTO:ARMORPROF|ARMORTYPE=Light	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.284	DESC:Proficient with all simple and martial weapons, light armor and shields (except tower shields).
Quick Turn	KEY:Horseman Fighter ~ Quick Turn	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantHorseman	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Horseman)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.284	DESC:Horseman special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). When charging on a mount he may make a number of turns (each 90 degrees or less) equal to the mount's Dexterity modifier, each needing a DC 15 Ride check, or the charge becomes a double move and the mount cannot attack.
Share Shield	KEY:Horseman Fighter ~ Share Shield	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantHorseman	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Horseman)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.284	DESC:Horseman special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). He shares his shield bonus with his mount as a move action with a successful DC 15 Ride check.
Spur	KEY:Horseman Fighter ~ Spur	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantHorseman	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Horseman)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.284	DESC:Horseman special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). He urges his mount to greater speed: +10 feet to its base speed for one round, a number of times per day equal to the mount's Constitution bonus.
Steady Hand	KEY:Horseman Fighter ~ Steady Hand	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantHorseman	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Horseman)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.284	DESC:Horseman special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). Whenever his mount must succeed on a Will save to overcome a mind-affecting effect, he may make a Ride check (DC 10 + the spell DC); on a success the mount's save succeeds.

###Block: Fighter (Janissary)
Fighter (Janissary)	KEY:Fighter (Janissary) ~ Class Description	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	VISIBLE:NO	SOURCEPAGE:p.285	DESC:A specialist fighter (Dragon Magazine Compendium variant fighter): Modeled on the Ottoman janissaries: conscripted children raised as fiercely loyal warriors, learned in arts beyond the martial, often speaking strange tongues; usually lawful. A janissary advances as a fighter (same Hit Die, base attack, saves, skill points, bonus feats); a character with fighter levels cannot take janissary levels or vice versa. Bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and every even level from the list of the Janissary Fighter Feat, or one of its special abilities in their place. Class skills: the fighter's plus Speak Language and two Knowledge skills of his choice; Handle Animal, Intimidate and Swim are cross-class. The compendium reprints only these changes from the janissary article (no further class features); appropriate feats include Blind-Fight, Combat Expertise, Improved Disarm, Improved Sunder and Combat Engineer.
Janissary Knowledge Skills	KEY:Janissary Fighter ~ Janissary Knowledge Skills	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	MULT:YES	CHOOSE:NUMCHOICES=2|SKILL|TYPE=Knowledge	CSKILL:LIST	SOURCEPAGE:p.285	DESC:Two Knowledge skills of his choice are class skills.

###Block: Fighter (Kensai)
Fighter (Kensai)	KEY:Fighter (Kensai) ~ Class Description	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	VISIBLE:NO	SOURCEPAGE:p.285	DESC:A specialist fighter (Dragon Magazine Compendium variant fighter): Warriors who train with a single melee weapon of their choice (sword, axe, mace, flail, spiked chain ...) and master it almost from the start. Bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and every even level from the list of the Kensai Fighter Feat, or one of its special abilities in their place. No bonus feat at 1st level (the chosen weapon bonus instead); weapon-specific bonus feats must name her chosen weapon (by hand). Not Complete Warrior's kensai prestige class.
Bonus Feats	KEY:Fighter (Kensai) ~ Bonus Feats	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	DEFINE:KensaiBonusFeatCount|0	BONUS:VAR|KensaiBonusFeatCount|floor(Kensai_FVLVL/2)	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Kensai Fighter Feat|KensaiBonusFeatCount	SOURCEPAGE:p.285	DESC:Bonus feats from the kensai list, or special abilities in their place (%1 now).|KensaiBonusFeatCount
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Fighter (Kensai) ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|TYPE=Simple	AUTO:ARMORPROF|ARMORTYPE=Light	SOURCEPAGE:p.285	DESC:Proficient with all simple weapons, light armor, and one martial or exotic melee weapon - her chosen weapon (Kensai Chosen Weapon).
Rain of Blows	KEY:Kensai Fighter ~ Rain of Blows	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantKensai	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Kensai)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.285	DESC:Kensai special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). When taking the full attack action with her chosen weapon she can take -3 on all attack rolls that round to make one additional melee attack with it at her highest attack bonus.
Storm of Blows	KEY:Kensai Fighter ~ Storm of Blows	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantKensai	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Kensai)=1	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Kensai Fighter ~ Rain of Blows	SOURCEPAGE:p.285	DESC:Kensai special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). When taking the full attack action with her chosen weapon she can take -6 on all attack rolls that round to make two additional melee attacks with it at her highest attack bonus. Requires rain of blows.
Chosen Weapon Bonus	KEY:Kensai Fighter ~ Chosen Weapon Bonus	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.285	DESC:Instead of a 1st-level bonus feat: +%1 on attack and damage rolls with her chosen weapon (+1 at 1st level, +1 at 5th and every five levels thereafter; by hand on the weapon).|1+floor(Kensai_FVLVL/5)
Kensai Chosen Weapon	KEY:Fighter (Kensai) ~ Kensai Chosen Weapon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Kensai Chosen Weapon|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.285	DESC:Her chosen weapon: proficiency with one martial or exotic melee weapon (melee only - by hand).

###Block: Fighter (Knight)
Fighter (Knight)	KEY:Fighter (Knight) ~ Class Description	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	VISIBLE:NO	SOURCEPAGE:p.286	DESC:A specialist fighter (Dragon Magazine Compendium variant fighter): Knights, good or bad, are the masters of mounted combat and command, the elite of noble soldiers, after many years of menial tasks as squires. Bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and every even level from the list of the Knight Fighter Feat, or one of its special abilities in their place. Not Player's Handbook II's knight base class.
Bonus Feats	KEY:Fighter (Knight) ~ Bonus Feats	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	DEFINE:KnightBonusFeatCount|0	BONUS:VAR|KnightBonusFeatCount|1+floor(Knight_FVLVL/2)	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Knight Fighter Feat|KnightBonusFeatCount	SOURCEPAGE:p.286	DESC:Bonus feats from the knight list, or special abilities in their place (%1 now).|KnightBonusFeatCount
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Fighter (Knight) ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|TYPE=Simple|TYPE=Martial	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.286	DESC:Proficient with all simple and martial weapons, all armor (heavy, medium and light) and shields (except tower shields).
Hard Charge	KEY:Knight Fighter ~ Hard Charge	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantKnight	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Knight)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.286	DESC:Knight special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). When he makes a mounted charge, his and his mount's attacks gain +2 on damage as long as the mount moved at least its speed.
Jousting Charge	KEY:Knight Fighter ~ Jousting Charge	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantKnight	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Knight)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.286	DESC:Knight special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). With a heavy or light shield readied when making a mounted charge he takes no -2 penalty to AC (his mount still does).
Staggered Gait	KEY:Knight Fighter ~ Staggered Gait	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantKnight	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Knight)=1	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Trample	SOURCEPAGE:p.286	DESC:Knight special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). When he successfully overruns an opponent with Trample, his mount may take -2 on all its attack rolls that round to gain a second hoof attack against the tripped opponent. Requires Trample.
Vicious Mount	KEY:Knight Fighter ~ Vicious Mount	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantKnight	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Knight)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.286	DESC:Knight special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). While he rides it, his mount's attacks gain +1 on damage.

###Block: Fighter (Pugilist)
Fighter (Pugilist)	KEY:Fighter (Pugilist) ~ Class Description	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	VISIBLE:NO	SOURCEPAGE:p.288	DESC:A specialist fighter (Dragon Magazine Compendium variant fighter): Pugilists do not waste time learning many weapons: they master the simplest of all, their own hands - boxers and brawlers. Bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and every even level from the list of the Pugilist Fighter Feat, or one of its special abilities in their place. Weapon-specific bonus feats must name unarmed strike (by hand).
Bonus Feats	KEY:Fighter (Pugilist) ~ Bonus Feats	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	DEFINE:PugilistBonusFeatCount|0	BONUS:VAR|PugilistBonusFeatCount|1+floor(Pugilist_FVLVL/2)	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Pugilist Fighter Feat|PugilistBonusFeatCount	SOURCEPAGE:p.288	DESC:Bonus feats from the pugilist list, or special abilities in their place (%1 now).|PugilistBonusFeatCount
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Fighter (Pugilist) ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|TYPE=Simple	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy	SOURCEPAGE:p.288	DESC:Proficient with all simple weapons and all armor (heavy, medium and light); no shields.
Combo	KEY:Pugilist Fighter ~ Combo	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantPugilist	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Pugilist)=1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	SOURCEPAGE:p.288	DESC:Pugilist special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). A series of blows each setting up the next: in a full attack she averages her first two unarmed strike attack bonuses and uses the result for both (+10/+5 becomes +7/+7); each further time she takes this ability, one more iterative attack joins the combo.
Heavy Hitting	KEY:Pugilist Fighter ~ Heavy Hitting	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantPugilist	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Pugilist)=1	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Pugilist)=2	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	SOURCEPAGE:p.288	DESC:Pugilist special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). Her unarmed strikes deal +2 extra nonlethal damage per time taken, even when she deals lethal damage. Not before 2nd level.
Iron Jaw	KEY:Pugilist Fighter ~ Iron Jaw	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantPugilist	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Pugilist)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.288	DESC:Pugilist special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). Nonlethal damage she takes is reduced by her Constitution bonus, and she gains +1 on saves against attacks that would stun her.
Shake it Off	KEY:Pugilist Fighter ~ Shake it Off	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantPugilist	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Pugilist)=1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	SOURCEPAGE:p.288	DESC:Pugilist special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). She reduces the duration of all stunning effects on her by 1 round per time taken (minimum 1 round); the effects stack.
Pugilist Training	KEY:Pugilist Fighter ~ Pugilist Training	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Improved Unarmed Strike	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Endurance	SOURCEPAGE:p.288	DESC:Improved Unarmed Strike and Endurance for free at 1st level (applied); her unarmed strikes deal 1d4 damage (1d3 if Small; applied).

###Block: Fighter (Shield Bearer)
Fighter (Shield Bearer)	KEY:Fighter (Shield Bearer) ~ Class Description	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	VISIBLE:NO	SOURCEPAGE:p.290	DESC:A specialist fighter (Dragon Magazine Compendium variant fighter): Fighters who make the shield their primary focus instead of their weapon, though certainly proficient with a blade. Bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and every even level from the list of the Shield Bearer Fighter Feat, or one of its special abilities in their place. Weapon-specific bonus feats must name a type of shield for shield bash attacks (by hand).
Bonus Feats	KEY:Fighter (Shield Bearer) ~ Bonus Feats	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	DEFINE:ShieldBearerBonusFeatCount|0	BONUS:VAR|ShieldBearerBonusFeatCount|floor(ShieldBearer_FVLVL/2)	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Shield Bearer Fighter Feat|ShieldBearerBonusFeatCount	SOURCEPAGE:p.290	DESC:Bonus feats from the shield bearer list, or special abilities in their place (%1 now).|ShieldBearerBonusFeatCount
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Fighter (Shield Bearer) ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|TYPE=Simple|TYPE=Martial|Spiked Armor	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy|TYPE=ShieldProfTower	SOURCEPAGE:p.290	DESC:Proficient with all simple and martial weapons, all armor (heavy, medium and light), shields (including tower shields) and armor spikes.
Armored Gait	KEY:Shield Bearer Fighter ~ Armored Gait	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantShieldBearer	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Shield Bearer)=1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	SOURCEPAGE:p.290	DESC:Shield Bearer special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). Choose one type of armor (such as a breastplate): it counts as one weight category lighter for her speed (medium armor does not slow her; heavy armor still does but she can run at four times her speed), not for abilities depending on the armor category. Each time taken it applies to a new type of armor (record the armor type by hand).
Armored Grace	KEY:Shield Bearer Fighter ~ Armored Grace	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantShieldBearer	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Shield Bearer)=1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	SOURCEPAGE:p.290	DESC:Shield Bearer special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). Choose one type of armor: its maximum Dexterity bonus increases by one when she wears it. Each time taken it applies to a new type of armor (record the armor type by hand).
Armor Optimization	KEY:Shield Bearer Fighter ~ Armor Optimization	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantShieldBearer	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Shield Bearer)=1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	SOURCEPAGE:p.290	DESC:Shield Bearer special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). Choose one type of armor: +1 to its armor bonus when she wears it, twisting to take blows on its most protective parts; lost whenever she is denied her Dexterity bonus to AC. Each time taken it applies to a new type of armor (record the armor type by hand).
Fortification	KEY:Shield Bearer Fighter ~ Fortification	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantShieldBearer	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Shield Bearer)=1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	SOURCEPAGE:p.290	DESC:Shield Bearer special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). Choose one type of armor: +2 to its armor bonus only against rolls to confirm critical hits (stacking with all other armor bonuses, including armor optimization). Each time taken it applies to a new type of armor (record the armor type by hand).
Shield Strike	KEY:Shield Bearer Fighter ~ Shield Strike	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantShieldBearer	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Shield Bearer)=1	SERVESAS:ABILITY=FEAT|Improved Unarmed Strike	SOURCEPAGE:p.290	DESC:Shield Bearer special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). She may use her shield in place of an unarmed attack for special maneuvers: Shield Strike counts as Improved Unarmed Strike for taking the feats of the unarmed chain (Stunning Fist, Deflect Arrows ...; applied), using a readied shield instead of a free hand.
Shield Bash Training	KEY:Shield Bearer Fighter ~ Shield Bash Training	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Improved Shield Bash	SOURCEPAGE:p.290	DESC:Her first fighter bonus feat must be Improved Shield Bash (granted automatically at 1st level in place of that selection).

###Block: Fighter (Survivalist)
Fighter (Survivalist)	KEY:Fighter (Survivalist) ~ Class Description	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	VISIBLE:NO	SOURCEPAGE:p.290	DESC:A specialist fighter (Dragon Magazine Compendium variant fighter): Not nature lovers: survivalists would rather stay within the walls of civilization, but they have learned to survive in the wilds when they must. Bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and every even level from the list of the Survivalist Fighter Feat, or one of its special abilities in their place. Skill Focus is limited to a survivalist class skill (by hand). The compendium lists no special abilities for the survivalist.
Bonus Feats	KEY:Fighter (Survivalist) ~ Bonus Feats	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	DEFINE:SurvivalistBonusFeatCount|0	BONUS:VAR|SurvivalistBonusFeatCount|1+floor(Survivalist_FVLVL/2)	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Survivalist Fighter Feat|SurvivalistBonusFeatCount	SOURCEPAGE:p.290	DESC:Bonus feats from the survivalist list, or special abilities in their place (%1 now).|SurvivalistBonusFeatCount
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Fighter (Survivalist) ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|TYPE=Simple|TYPE=Martial	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ArmorProfMedium|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.290	DESC:Proficient with all simple and martial weapons, light and medium armor and shields (except tower shields).

###Block: Fighter (Targetteer)
Fighter (Targetteer)	KEY:Fighter (Targetteer) ~ Class Description	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	VISIBLE:NO	SOURCEPAGE:p.291	DESC:A specialist fighter (Dragon Magazine Compendium variant fighter): Beyond archers and marksmen: the targetteer focuses on the totality of ranged combat rather than one weapon. Bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and every even level from the list of the Targetteer Fighter Feat, or one of its special abilities in their place. 
Bonus Feats	KEY:Fighter (Targetteer) ~ Bonus Feats	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	DEFINE:TargetteerBonusFeatCount|0	BONUS:VAR|TargetteerBonusFeatCount|1+floor(Targetteer_FVLVL/2)	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Targetteer Fighter Feat|TargetteerBonusFeatCount	SOURCEPAGE:p.291	DESC:Bonus feats from the targetteer list, or special abilities in their place (%1 now).|TargetteerBonusFeatCount
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Fighter (Targetteer) ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|TYPE=Simple|TYPE=Martial.Ranged	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy	AUTO:SHIELDPROF|Buckler	SOURCEPAGE:p.291	DESC:Proficient with all simple weapons, all ranged martial weapons, all armor (light, medium and heavy) and the buckler, and with two ranged exotic weapons chosen at 1st level (Targetteer Exotic Weapons).
Arrow Swarm	KEY:Targetteer Fighter ~ Arrow Swarm	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantTargetteer	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Targetteer)=1	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Rapid Shot	SOURCEPAGE:p.291	DESC:Targetteer special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). Making a full attack, he takes -5 on all attack rolls for a round to make two additional ranged attacks at his highest attack bonus. Requires Rapid Shot.
Sniper	KEY:Targetteer Fighter ~ Sniper	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantTargetteer	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Targetteer)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.291	DESC:Targetteer special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). In a full attack he can sacrifice attacks for deadly accuracy: each sacrificed attack increases the threat range of his next ranged attack by 1 (19-20 becomes 18-20, and so on); he cannot sacrifice all his attacks.
Vital Aim	KEY:Targetteer Fighter ~ Vital Aim	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:FighterVariantTargetteer	PRECLASS:1,Fighter (Targetteer)=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.291	DESC:Targetteer special ability (taken in place of a bonus feat). He may add his Dexterity modifier to ranged weapon damage instead of his Strength bonus (a Strength penalty is replaced only by a Dexterity penalty); not against creatures immune to critical hits.
Targetteer Exotic Weapons	KEY:Fighter (Targetteer) ~ Targetteer Exotic Weapons	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Targetteer Exotic Weapons|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.291	DESC:Two exotic weapon proficiencies at 1st level - ranged weapons only (by hand).

###Block: Fighter (Thane)
Fighter (Thane)	KEY:Fighter (Thane) ~ Class Description	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	VISIBLE:NO	SOURCEPAGE:p.291	DESC:A specialist fighter (Dragon Magazine Compendium variant fighter): Professional fighters sworn to protect a clan or tribal chieftain - bodyguards, companions and commanders of their liege's warbands, expected to die defending or avenging their liege. A thane is a specialist fighter, much like an evoker is a specialist wizard: he advances as a fighter (same Hit Die, base attack, saves, skill points, proficiencies, bonus feats); a character with fighter levels cannot take thane levels or vice versa. Bonus feats at 1st, 2nd and every even level from the list of the Thane Fighter Feat, or one of its special abilities in their place. Besides the normal fighter bonus feats he may also select Aura of Bravery, Improved Aid Another and Stalwart as fighter bonus feats (feats from other books, not in the repository - by hand).
Thane's Vow	KEY:Thane Fighter ~ Thane's Vow	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Fighter Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.291	DESC:At 1st level he devotes himself to a single lord who accepts his service, and can never voluntarily change lords. If his lord is killed he must avenge him or die trying, as if under geas/quest (not ended by remove curse); a lordless thane takes -4 on all Charisma-based skill checks until he fulfills his vow, after which he must devote himself to a new lord.

